# Clear Glass gig file (clearglass.gig/1) — load it in Settings → Autofill → Gig, or in the gig panel.
format: clearglass.gig/1
platform: fiverr
title: I will build a custom Electron desktop app for Windows or Mac
category: Programming & Tech
subcategory: Software Development
serviceType: ''
tags:
  - electron
  - desktop app
  - windows app
  - node.js
  - javascript
description: >-
  Need a desktop app for your team or your own work? I build Electron apps that look clean, run on
  Windows and Mac, and are easy to update.


  My own daily browser is an Electron app I direct: custom windows and title bars, background tasks,
  local storage, and automation built in. Your app gets the same care at the size you need.


  What I can build:

  - A desktop tool around your workflow or your data

  - A desktop wrapper for a web app you already have

  - Local file processing, tray apps and background tasks

  - Custom, dark or branded windows and title bars


  What you get:

  - A working app with an installer

  - The source code with a readme

  - A short demo of every feature you asked for


  How it works: you describe the screens and what each does. I confirm the plan, build it, and show
  you each part working before delivery.
packages:
  basic:
    name: Simple Tool
    description: A one-screen desktop tool with an installer.
    deliveryDays: 4
    revisions: 1
    price: 120
  standard:
    name: Multi-Screen App
    description: Up to 4 screens, local storage, installer and readme.
    deliveryDays: 8
    revisions: 2
    price: 320
  premium:
    name: Full Desktop App
    description: Custom windows, background tasks, auto-update and tests.
    deliveryDays: 14
    revisions: 3
    price: 700
faq:
  - question: Windows, Mac or both?
    answer: Both are possible. Tell me which you need; I test on the ones you choose.
  - question: Can it use my existing website?
    answer: Yes. I can wrap an existing web app, or build the screens from scratch.
  - question: Do I get the source code?
    answer: Yes, all of it, with a readme on how to build and run it.
requirements:
  - 'Describe the app: what screens does it need, and what does each one do?'
  - Who will use it, and on what? (Windows, Mac, a server; one person or a team)
  - What must it always do, and what must it never do?
  - How will you check that it is done? (the test you will run, or what you will look at)
  - Please share any files, examples, access or data I need to start.
metadata:
  Programming language:
    - JavaScript
